      "content": "That whistling or whining sound is primarily due to the extremely high velocity of the air moving through the compressor blades. The rapid movement and pressure differentials across these spinning components create the characteristic aerodynamic noise. While it is air movement, the intense pressure changes and turbulence at those speeds are what generate the high-pitched sound you hear.",
