      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, abnormal sounds are a strong indicator of trouble with the turbocharger. Debris impacting the compressor or turbine wheels can cause erratic rattling or scraping sounds, which are very different from normal whistling. If the bearings are failing, you might hear whining, grinding, or howling sounds, as the physical components begin to wear out or vibrate excessively under pressure. These changes in sound quality suggest mechanical failure requiring inspection.",
